  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let a curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;pass through the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>. If the tangent at any point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;to the given curve cuts the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to _____.</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>A curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;pass through the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p>And the tangent at any point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;to the given curve cuts the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></math></p><p>Now tangent to the curve is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Now at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis, put&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;as point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;given,</p><p>Now given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;{here <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;on the curve}</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>d</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi><mfenced><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p>Now integrating both side we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></math>,&nbsp;</p><p>Now given curve passes through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>, so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>So, equation of curve will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Now curve also passes through the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So, by distance formula we get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}